        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "In conclusion, we have developed a practical, mild, and convenient procedure for the synthesis of propiolaldehyde using molecular oxygen as oxidant under atmospheric pressure at room temperature with a higher yield. "
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                77,
                131,
                489,
                191
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "1 H and 13C NMR spectra were recorded with an instrument operated at 300 MHz for 1 H NMR and 75 MHz for 13C NMR in "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "{ \\mathrm { \\hat { C } D C l } } _ { 3 } ."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Chemical shifts (δ) are given in parts per million (ppm). IR spectra were recorded on an FT IR spectrometer. Mass spectra were recorded in EI mode. Fe(NO3)3·9H2O, NaCl, and p-xylene were purchased from Sinopharm Chemical Reagent Corporation; TEMPO (purity: 99%) was purchased from AstaTech Pharmaceutical Corporation; propargyl alcohol (purity: 98%) was available from Shanghai Darui Fine Chemical Corporation. "
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                77,
                207,
                489,
                317
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Propiolaldehyde (1) "
                    }
                ],
                "level": 1
            },
            "bbox": [
                78,
                325,
                211,
                337
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "A three-necked 2000 mL round-bottomed flask equipped with a thermometer and a pressure-equalizing addition funnel was fitted with a magnetic stirring bar. To this flask were added Fe(NO3)3·9H2O (20.20 g, 50.0 mmol), TEMPO (4.70 g, 30.0 mmol), NaCl (2.91 g, 50 mmol), and p-xylene (1000 mL) under the atmosphere of air at r.t. The air atmosphere was then replaced with oxygen by an oxygen bag commonly used in hospitals (SY-42 L, Shanghai Sanhe Medical Instrument CO., Ltd) (Figure 1). Propargyl alcohol (58.0 mL, d = 0.949, 55.85 g, 1.0 mol) was injected via a syringe and then added to the suspension through the addition funnel dropwise with stirring at r.t. within ~1 h. After stirring at r.t. for an additional 4 h (note: the reaction was exothermic, so the internal temperature would rise up to "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "4 5 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ;"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "care must be taken to keep the temperature <45 °C), the reaction was complete as monitored by 1 H NMR analysis (300 MHz, CDCl3) till the signals for the starting alcohol (δ = 4.24, d, J = 2.4 Hz, 2 H, CH2) disappeared. The resulting liquid layer was separated, and the residue was washed with p-xylene (2 × 50 mL). The combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4) and filtered through a short pad of silica gel (Φ 7 cm × 1 cm). The filtrate was transferred to a 2 L round-bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirring bar and distilled through a Liebig condenser (20 "
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                77,
                337,
                489,
                587
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "image",
            "content": {
                "image_source": {
                    "path": "images/fc3e59c8bf296ca66b7238a79a6bc662ee1e21093213ac38323ffaf427102081.jpg"
                },
                "content": "Laboratory setup with glassware and a blue cushion, no visible text or symbols",
                "image_caption": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Figure 1 The reaction apparatus used for the aerobic oxidation of propargyl alcohol "
                    }
                ],
                "image_footnote": []
            },
            "sub_type": "natural_image",
            "bbox": [
                82,
                618,
                487,
                834
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "cm) under atmospheric pressure to afford propiolaldehyde (38.78 g, bp 53–83 °C/760 mm Hg) containing about 12–23% of the solvent. Redistillation led to the collection of pure propiolaldehyde;13 yield: 30.06 g (54%); bp 54–57 °C/760 mm Hg; purity: 94%. The purity was determined by GC. Conditions: column: HP-5 (25 m × 0.32 mm); carrier: N2; injector: "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "2 5 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ;"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "detector (FID, H2): 250 °C; flow: 50 °C for 5 min, 3 °C/min to 150 °C and hold for 5 min; tR = 1.4 min (propiolaldehyde, 94%), "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "t _ { \\mathrm { R } } = 5 . 1"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "min (p-xylene, 5%). "
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                505,
                58,
                917,
                155
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Note: The product should be stored in a bottle with a glass-stopper, since contaminants from a rubber stopper may be sufficient to catalyze decomposition. "
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                505,
                157,
